<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich Himmler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich Himmler was Reichsführer of the SS from 1929 and from 1936 chief of all German police, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gestapo">Gestapo</a>. He built the SS into a state within the state that ran the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>, and he was the principal organiser of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> and of the murder of millions of others. Captured by British troops in May 1945, he killed himself with poison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-himmler.jpg" alt="Heinrich Himmler" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Franz Bauer · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_Himmler_(3x4_cropped)_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
